      "text": "To solve the given problem, we start with the equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\) and need to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\).\n\nFirst, let's denote the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) by \\(S\\). So we have:\n\\[ S = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1. \\]\n\nWe can express \\(S\\) in a different form by factoring out common terms. Notice that:\n\\[ S = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1} \\quad \\text{for} \\quad x \\neq 1. \\]\n\nFrom the given equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rewrite it as:\n\\[ x^{2017} = 2x - 1. \\]\n\nSubstituting \\(x^{2017} = 2x - 1\\) into the expression for \\(S\\), we get:\n\\[ S = \\frac{2x - 1 - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2, \\]\nprovided that \\(x \\neq 1\\).\n\nThus, the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
