      "text": "Given the polynomial equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we are to find the value of the sum \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\).\n\nFirst, let's denote the sum by \\(S\\):\n\\[ S = x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1. \\]\n\nWe can factor out a power of \\(x\\) from the series:\n\\[ S = \\frac{x^{2017} - 1}{x - 1}, \\]\nwhere we subtract 1 from the numerator because the sum of a geometric series \\(x^n + x^{n-1} + \\dots + x + 1\\) can be represented by \\(\\frac{x^n - 1}{x - 1}\\).\n\nFrom the given equation \\(x^{2017} - 2x + 1 = 0\\), we can rearrange it to:\n\\[ x^{2017} = 2x - 1. \\]\n\nUsing this, we substitute \\(x^{2017}\\) in the expression for \\(S\\):\n\\[ S = \\frac{2x - 1 - 1}{x - 1} = \\frac{2x - 2}{x - 1} = \\frac{2(x - 1)}{x - 1} = 2. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(x^{2016} + x^{2015} + \\dots + x + 1\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
